-- title:
--   Vanishing multidegree of a divisorially presented bundle on the resolved model
-- statement:
--   Fix $N_0 \neq 0$ and a prime $p$ with $p \nmid N_0$, a Deligne–Rapoport model package $\mathfrak{P}$ of level $N_0p$ over the base ring `DRLevel.R p`, a relative $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ designation $D$ for the structure morphism `DRLevel.toBase N₀ p` (a scheme $D.P$ with a morphism to the base and a zero section), and a witness $hD$ that $D$ represents the sub-Picard condition `algEquivZeroCut`, i.e. the condition on rigidified line bundles that every geometric fibre bundle is algebraically equivalent to zero; $hD$ supplies in particular a Poincaré bundle over $D.P$. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain with $\mathrm{ho}\,$maximal ideal generated by the image of $p$, $\rho_O : \mathrm{DRLevel.R}\ p \to O$ a ring map, $\kappa$ an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$ with a surjective ring map $O \to \kappa$, and $\mathfrak{X}^{\mathrm{reg}}$ a resolved model package `DRResolvedModelPackageLevel N₀ p 𝔓 O ρO κ toκ`, with total space $Y$, structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} O$, a proper morphism `toDR` to the base change of the Deligne–Rapoport model along $\rho_O$, a finite set of nodes with widths, and invertible ideal sheaves $\mathfrak{X}^{\mathrm{reg}}.\mathrm{comp}\,v$ indexed by the components $v$ in `X0MqComponents 𝔛reg.width` $= \mathrm{Fin}\,2 \sqcup \coprod_n \mathrm{Fin}(\mathrm{width}(n)-1)$, whose product cuts out $p$. Let $z$ be an $O$-point of $D.P$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\rho_O$, let $\sigma_0,\dots,\sigma_{m-1}$ be sections of $Y \to \operatorname{Spec} O$, let $\mathrm{pos}, \mathrm{neg} : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \mathbb{N}$, and let $v_j$ be the unique component whose support contains the image of the closed point of $O$ under $\sigma_j$ (this uniqueness being the hypothesis $hv$). Let $a^+, a^- : \text{components} \to \mathbb{N}$, and assume the pullback along `toDR` of the line bundle of the Poincaré bundle pulled back along $z$ is isomorphic to the iterated tensor product over $j = 0,\dots,m-1$ of the dual of $(\ker \sigma_j)^{\mathrm{pos}\,j}$ and of $(\ker \sigma_j)^{\mathrm{neg}\,j}$, tensored with the dual of $\prod_F (\mathrm{comp}\,F)^{a^+(F)}$ and with $\prod_F (\mathrm{comp}\,F)^{a^-(F)}$, each ideal sheaf being regarded as a sheaf of modules and duals formed internally. Then for every component $c$, $$\sum_j [v_j = c]\,(\mathrm{pos}\,j - \mathrm{neg}\,j) + \sum_F (a^+(F) - a^-(F))\cdot \mathrm{inter}(F, c) = 0,$$ where the intersection numbers are those of the table `x0MqResolvedTable 𝔛reg.width`: all multiplicities $1$, off-diagonal entry the adjacency number `x0MqAdj`, and diagonal entry minus the sum of the adjacencies in the row.
--
--   This is the statement that a line bundle lying in the algebraically-trivial part of the relative Picard functor has vanishing multidegree on the special fibre of the resolved model of $X_0(N_0p)$ over $O$: the contribution of the horizontal part $\sum_j(\mathrm{pos}_j-\mathrm{neg}_j)\sigma_j$ at each component cancels against the intersection pairing of the vertical part $\sum_F (a^+_F-a^-_F)C_F$ with that component. It feeds the description of the image of the intersection matrix in the component-group computation for the resolved model, used by `multidegree_mem_range_intersectionAlpha_of_pullbackAlong_generic_iso_of_surjective`.
